# Gideon, Battle-Forged: "+2: Up to one target creature an opponent controls attacks Gideon during its controller's next
# turn if able" (CR 508.1d, 611.2a). Kytheon transforms on turn 3 and the +2 targets Bot2's Dwarven Mauler - not Bot1's own
# Ornithopter, which is not a creature an opponent controls. Bot1 then takes an extra turn with Time Walk (turn 4): Bot1's
# next turn comes and goes, and Bot2's does not. On turn 5, Bot2's next turn, the Mauler must attack Gideon: attacking Bot1
# instead, or not attacking, is refused, and its 2 damage takes Gideon from 5 loyalty to 3. On turn 7 the requirement is
# over (it ended once both players had begun a turn since) and the Mauler attacks Bot1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Kytheon, Hero of Akros
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Black Lotus
Time Walk
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Dwarven Mauler
Mountain x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Kytheon, Hero of Akros.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Dwarven Mauler.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Kytheon, Hero of Akros > Bot2; Ornithopter#1 > Bot2; Ornithopter#2 > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
! Bot1.Battlefield.Gideon, Battle-Forged.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter; Ability: +2)
Bot1.Battlefield.Gideon, Battle-Forged.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.Dwarven Mauler; Ability: +2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Dwarven Mauler.MustAttack = Gideon, Battle-Forged
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Time Walk.Cast
[T4 Bot1.Main2]
? ActivePlayer = Bot1
[T5 Bot2.Main1]
! Bot2.Attack(Dwarven Mauler > Bot1)
! Bot2.Attack()
[T5 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Gideon, Battle-Forged.Counters.Loyalty = 3
[T7 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Dwarven Mauler.MustAttack = (absent)
Bot2.Attack(Dwarven Mauler > Bot1)
[T7 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 18
Bot1.Battlefield.Gideon, Battle-Forged.Counters.Loyalty = 3
